We need to design dynamic pricing evaluation engine.

We have a parking lot and parking lot manager can define there own set of rules for fare calculations
like night charges, weekend charges, festival charges and upper cap for fare per day for different types of vehicles.

The core requirements would be defining an interface for dynamic rule creation, where clients can define conditions—like
vehicle type or time of day—and associated actions. Your system must maintain a rule registry to store these configurations
and provide an evaluation engine that processes an input context—like entry and exit times—against the active rules to
compute the final charge.

Example to understand the problem statement:

Parking ticket:
Entry time, exit time, Vehicle type

Fee Rules can be like:
MAX_FREE_HOUR
PARKING_FEE
FEE_UPPEAR_LIMIT
WEEKEND_CHARGES
NIGHT_CHARGES
FESTIVAL_CHARGES

Example:
1. First hour is free
2. Bike - 20 rs / hour
3. Car - 40 rs / hour
4. Truck - 60 rs / hour
5. Upper cap for a day (24 hours) :
Bike - 200 rs
Car - 400 rs
Truck - 600 rs

Need to make rules configurable.
Can onboard N vehicle with N type of rules to calculate fare.
How to handle race conditions?